  "chapter": 727,
  "signer": "KATHY HOCHUL",
  "text": " \n                APPROVAL MEMORANDUM - No. 48 Chapter 727\n \n      MEMORANDUM filed with Assembly Bill Number 3217-A, entitled:\n \n    \"AN  ACT  to amend the public service law and the public authorities\n        law, in relation to defining medical needs for  essential  elec-\n        tricity  and  to  require  certain  service providers' emergency\n        response plans to include outreach plans for customers who  have\n        documented  their  need  for  essential  electricity for medical\n        needs\"\n \n    APPROVED\n \n  This bill elaborates on  the  medical  equipment  that  qualifies  for\nessential  electricity  for  medical needs under the Public Service Law.\nThis bill would require electric companies to identify and reach out  to\ncustomers  that  use  such  equipment  and  who  would  be significantly\naffected by a loss of power. The Public Service Commission  has  adopted\nand  recently  updated  regulations  (16  NYCRR  Section 105.4(b)(9)) to\nfurther define lifesaving equipment in utility Emergency Response  Plans\n(ERPs). These regulations provide the specificity that would be required\nunder this bill.\n \n  Ensuring  New  Yorkers do not lose power to vital medical equipment or\nother lifesaving essential equipment is of  utmost  importance.  I  have\nsecured  an  agreement with the Legislature to make technical changes to\nclarify language  related  to  what  equipment  is  lifesaving  for  the\npurposes of this legislation.\n \n  Based on this agreement, I am pleased to sign this bill into law.\n \n  This bill is approved.                         (signed) KATHY HOCHUL\n \n                                ______\n",
  "year": 2022
 },
